b24 — a Bitrix24 portal's CRM in a local store, for scripts and agents, with a permission on every
write.

Usage: b24 <profile> <command> [options]
Account commands start with your profile, a name you choose; none is ever assumed.

What you can do:
  sync                               copy the portal's deals, leads, contacts and companies; the next sync takes the changes
  deals list status:open             open deals with stage, amount and owner, from the store, offline
  search all "kitchen"               stored deals and leads beside your other WireCat tools' data
  deals move <ref> <stage>           move a deal; deals.move=readonly stops agents moving one
  api call <method> --dry-run        any REST method, with every permission it checks
  mcp serve --permission deals=deny  the CRM in any agent, with the levels you set

Works with:
  tg                                 Telegram in the same local store: search, review and tasks offline
  max                                MAX in the same local store: search, review and tasks offline
  wa                                 WhatsApp in the same local store: search, review and tasks offline
  zm                                 Zoom meetings: transcripts and summaries, searchable with your other WireCat data
  drive                              Google Drive and Docs as local text, searchable with your other WireCat data
  gcal                               Google Calendar events, searchable with your other WireCat data
  memo context <person>              one person across messengers, mail, notes and meetings
  mail                               IMAP mail in the same local store: search your mailbox offline, next to your other WireCat data

Start here:   b24 work session start  (any profile name works)
Next:         b24 commands            every command, by section
              b24 guide               scenarios: command sequences for common tasks
              b24 help options        output, offline, timeouts, dry run
For agents:   b24 skill show          rules and the discovery loop
